Sergio can make technology look simple, accessible, and approachable while also translating the human need for engineers. It's all in pursuit of what he's passionate about: helping companies unlock that internal confidence they need to become more resilient and digitally fit in an increasingly circular economy.

As a Design Director at IDEO Europe based in London, Sergio sees product design as a way to shape behavior and lead to systemic change. He works with clients to turn what can be fixed environments into innovative ones populated with new skills—the kind needed to transition to more circular models and practices.

He got a taste of IDEO as a client before joining the company, where he has helped one of the biggest fashion retailers in the world redesign its supply chain to make it more sustainable and efficient by having their teams collaborate better. What started as a high-level idea was ideated, tested, and implemented, with real tangible impact on the supply chain, in less than a year.
Sergio started coding as a kid and spent his early career as a software engineer for tech start-ups before taking a job as business engineer lead for Yoox Net-a-Porter Group. He led a fast-paced team tasked with getting things done quickly, and it marked the point where he started to move away from the keyboard and toward the application of technology to solve for human-led needs.
